 "notes": [
  "P0 animatic v3 (MP4 review + OGV runtime + poster) verified against checkpoint 16 SHAs (outputs v3 manifest); 5 panels revised in total (4 in checkpoint 13: CIN_001_S03, CIN_001_S06, CIN_004_S01, CIN_004_S03; 1 in checkpoint 16: CIN_002_S02), 7 panels byte-identical to v1; poster unchanged (CIN_001_S01). Separate 16:9 keyframes per shot in Art_Source/Cinematics/P0_Animatic/keyframes_16x9/ (P0_keyframes_16x9_manifest_v1.json).",
  "Timing JSON + SRT per scene copied from Narrative/Deliveries with sha256 verification against the checkpoint 01/05/06 manifests. SRT is UTF-8/NFC, DRAFT.",
  "dialogueCues is derived from parsed timing JSON shots[].dialogue, cross-checked against the parsed SRT cue count and, where present, the source manifest 'cues' list (Gói 30 item 1 / PR119 review finding 1). P0 + CIN_006 source manifests carry no 'cues' key; their counts come from timing/SRT. Any disagreement aborts this build.",
  "Only CIN_001_S05 (24.8-28.5 s, version B) is DECIDED; all other dialogue windows remain PROPOSED_ANIMATIC_PLACEMENT until director/Codex confirms them.",
  "No final picture: animatic is storyboard level (revision v3 fixes all 5 recorded panel defects, not final picture); character keyframes still await lock for locked shots.",
  "Per-scene clips (checkpoint 18, Goi 30 item 6): CIN_001 (36 s), CIN_002 (18 s) and CIN_004 (18 s) each exported as its own MP4 + OGV + poster + SRT + timing + hash manifest under assets/cinematics/<SCENE>/. The 72 s reel stays review/gallery only, NOT auto-run as opening.",
  "CIN_005 animated take (checkpoint 21, Goi 30 item 7): first campaign video with real motion -- 18 s / 3 shots, slow Ken Burns camera moves on 3 storyboard keyframes (Art_Source/Cinematics/Campaign/CIN_005/keyframes_16x9/, CIN005_keyframes_manifest_v1.json). Animatic-level motion, NOT a final pose-animated take; no audio track in the clip (VO/music/ambience added separately in editing); no baked subtitles. Known defect: S02 roof palette drifts from S01.",
  "CIN_006 animated take (checkpoint 22, Goi 30 item 7): the scene leaves PENDING_PANELS_NO_STORYBOARD with 3 storyboard keyframes (Art_Source/Cinematics/Campaign/CIN_006/keyframes_16x9/, CIN006_keyframes_manifest_v1.json) + 18 s Ken Burns clip. NPC_HA_MAC / NPC_SAM_CHU_QUY have NO approved character lock: faces/costumes are storyboard placeholders, cinematic-only staging per DEC-MEDIA-P0 Q4. Known defects: S02 composition (oversized blurred glove + pale face-like shape at frame right) and cross-shot lighting drift, recorded per shot for the final-picture revision pass.",
  "CIN_009 animated take (checkpoint 23, Goi 30 item 7): first Chapter 2 campaign scene with video -- 18 s / 3 shots, slow Ken Burns camera moves on 3 storyboard keyframes (Art_Source/Cinematics/Campaign/CIN_009/keyframes_16x9/, CIN009_keyframes_manifest_v1.json). Pack character list is empty, so no character lock is involved; the S02 workers are unnamed generation-invented figures. Animatic-level motion, NOT a final pose-animated take; no audio track in the clip (VO/music/ambience added separately in editing); no baked subtitles. Known defects: S01 carries an invented white hooded figure not in the prompt and reads darker than a daylight payoff; S03 is not strictly top-down and adds a shrine not in the prompt.",
  "CIN_020 animated take (checkpoint 24, Goi 30 item 7): the closing campaign scene -- 18 s / 3 shots, slow Ken Burns camera moves on 3 storyboard keyframes (Art_Source/Cinematics/Campaign/CIN_020/keyframes_16x9/, CIN020_keyframes_manifest_v1.json). Pack character list is empty, so no character lock is involved; the villager is an unnamed figure. Animatic-level motion, NOT a final pose-animated take; no audio track in the clip; no baked subtitles. Known defects: the same villager wears three different outfits/headgear across the shots (continuity drift) and S02 is an interior medium shot instead of a detail close view. Also fixed in this checkpoint: the CIN_009 keyframe manifest carried CIN_006's title ('Con dau qua pho') since checkpoint 23 -- corrected to 'Tieng rung duoc dap' in the manifest and its builder.",
  "Campaign video batch (checkpoint 25, Goi 30 item 7): the remaining 13 campaign scenes (CIN_003, CIN_007, CIN_008, CIN_010, CIN_011, CIN_012, CIN_013, CIN_014, CIN_015, CIN_016, CIN_017, CIN_018, CIN_019) each gained an 18 s animated take -- slow Ken Burns camera moves on 3 storyboard keyframes per scene, generated in parallel staging runs from the pack shot prompts verbatim (Art_Source/Cinematics/Campaign/<scene>/keyframes_16x9/ + per-scene keyframe manifests; builder build_campaign_batch_video.py). All 20 scenes now carry video. Every batch scene has named characters on screen with NO approved cinematic character lock, so all batch faces/costumes are storyboard placeholders and final picture per shot stays blocked on the lock; animatic-level motion, NOT final pose-animated takes; no audio track in the clips; no baked subtitles. Headline recorded defects (full per-shot records in the keyframe manifests): CIN_012_S03 carries a baked-in game choice UI bar with legible English buttons (hard clean-frame violation); CIN_017_S02 misses its subject entirely (no crystal core, no serpent; invented robed man); CIN_015_S02 is a dry above-water courtyard instead of the drowned ruin, with an invented mascot figure (the same white hooded mascot-like intrusion also appears in CIN_012_S01); CIN_011 invents a design-consistent teal-robed woman in S01 and S03 who is in no prompt; CIN_010's environment collapses after S01 (desert -> bamboo grove -> scrub) and its Sam is a slim young man, not the stocky middle-aged merchant of the brief; CIN_008_S03's bandage reads on the character's right forearm while canon places it on the LEFT; CIN_018 has two dialogue cues and its S03 VO draft still overruns its window by +0.280 s (owner decision 2026-11-06: window kept as-is, Codex decides at PR review).",
  "Prologue film CIN_000 (checkpoint 27): a standalone 87.367 s pre-game lore film (owner-ordered; narration script approved in main chat 2026-11-06), registered under the separate 'prologue' key -- it is NOT one of the 20 campaign scenes and is not counted in campaignTotals. Unlike the campaign clips it CARRIES its mixed soundtrack (narration + composed theme + ambience) embedded in the MP4/OGV. Picture: 11 painterly cinematic panels + a code-rendered title card (poster = the title card). Canon guardrails: no avatar origin/face/bloodline, no naming of Co Vo Tuong / the hop mach mechanism / Ta Van Khanh's responsibility (reveal table), the traveler is an unnamed back-view silhouette, and the film ends on the checkpoint 04 CIN_001_S05 line (reused take) so it hands off into CIN_001. Recorded defects include the S01/S03 mechanism design drift and S11's ambiguous arrival direction (full per-shot records in CIN000_keyframes_manifest_v1.json). Wiring the prologue into the post-character-creation flow is Codex's presentation-adapter work."
 ],
